\"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned lines list is empty\",\n     \"when\": \"CartStore.addPart(part) is called\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Find parts lists a part with stock 0\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The button is shown disabled and pressing it leaves the header cart count value unchanged\",\n     \"when\": \"the buyer views or tabs to that part's \\\"Add to cart\\\" button\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a part is out of stock, then the portal shall disable its \\\"Add to cart\\\" button.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A CartStore holding 3 of part BP-200 \\\"Brake Pad\\\" at £12.50\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned line has name \\\"Brake Pad\\\", partNumber \\\"BP-200\\\", unitPrice 12.50, quantity 3 and lineTotal 37.50\",\n     \"when\": \"CartStore.lines() is called\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The cart shall give each line its name, part number, unit price, quantity and line total, where line total = unit price × quantity.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A CartStore holding 1 of a £12.50 part and 1 of a £5.00 part\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned lineTotal for that line is 50.00 and CartStore.subtotal() returns 55.00\",\n     \"when\": \"CartStore.setQuantity(\\\"BP-200\\\", 4) is called for the £12.50 part\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The Cart screen with a line at quantity 1\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The line total and the order total shown update without pressing any other button\",\n     \"when\": \"the buyer types 4 in the quantity field\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the buyer changes a line quantity, the cart shall recalculate that line total and the order totals at once.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A CartStore line for a part with stock 500\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned quantity values are 1, 1, 99 and 3\",\n     \"when\": \"CartStore.setQuantity is called with \\\"\\\", 0, 150 and 2.6 in turn\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If the buyer enters a quantity that is blank, 0, above 99 or not a whole number, then the cart shall set it to the nearest whole number from 1 to 99.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"ASM-12\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A CartStore line for a part with stock 4\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned quantity value is 4 and the returned message is \\\"Only 4 available\\\"\",\n     \"when\": \"CartStore.setQuantity(partNumber, 7) is called\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The Cart screen with a line for a part with stock 4\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The field shows 4 and \\\"Only 4 available\\\" is displayed next to the line\",\n     \"when\": \"the buyer types 7 in the quantity field\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If the buyer enters a quantity above the part's stock, then the cart shall set the quantity to the stock quantity and give the message \\\"Only n available\\\".\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A CartStore with lines BP-200 and OF-100\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned lines list contains only OF-100 and CartStore.count() returns OF-100's quantity\",\n     \"when\": \"CartStore.removeLine(\\\"BP-200\\\") is called\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the buyer presses \\\"Remove\\\" on a cart line, the cart shall remove that line.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A CartStore for buyer B1 holding 2 of OF-100, using a given local storage\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned list holds 2 of OF-100\",\n     \"when\": \"a new CartStore is created for buyer B1 with the same local storage and lines() is called\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The same local storage holding buyer B1's cart\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.2\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned list is empty\",\n     \"when\": \"a new CartStore is created for buyer B2 and lines() is called\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The cart shall keep its lines in the browser's local storage under the signed-in buyer's ID, so the cart survives page reloads on the same device.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"ASM-4\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A buyer with an empty cart\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"\\\"Your cart is empty\\\" and a link to /parts are shown, and no address field, delivery option or \\\"Place order\\\" button is displayed\",\n     \"when\": \"they open /cart\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"While the cart is empty, the portal shall show \\\"Your cart is empty\\\" with a link to Find parts and hide checkout.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A CheckoutForm with delivery option Standard\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned values are false, true, true and false\",\n     \"when\": \"CheckoutForm.canPlaceOrder() is called with addresses of 4, 5, 200 and 201 characters in turn\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A CheckoutForm with a 20-character address and no delivery option\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned value is false\",\n     \"when\": \"CheckoutForm.canPlaceOrder() is called\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A buyer who placed an earlier order\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.3\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The delivery address field is shown empty\",\n     \"when\": \"they open checkout again\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The checkout shall enable \\\"Place order\\\" only when the delivery address has 5 to 200 characters and a delivery option (Standard or Next day) is selected.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"ASM-15\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A CartStore with subtotal 37.50\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned value is subtotal 37.50, deliveryCharge 9.99, total 47.49\",\n     \"when\": \"CartStore.totals(\\\"NEXT_DAY\\\") is called\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A CartStore with subtotal 37.50\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.2\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned value is subtotal 37.50, deliveryCharge 0.00, total 37.50\",\n     \"when\": \"CartStore.totals(\\\"STANDARD\\\") is called\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The checkout shall show subtotal, delivery charge (Standard £0.00, Next day £9.99) and total, where total = subtotal + delivery charge.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"ASM-7\",\n    \"ASM-9\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Buyer B1, no earlier orders in the database, part BP-200 at £12.50 with stock 10\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response body has orderNumber \\\"ORD-000001\\\", status \\\"Placed\\\" and total 34.99\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 calls POST /api/orders with lines [{partNumber: BP-200, quantity: 2}], address \\\"1 High St, Leeds\\\", deliveryOption NEXT_DAY\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The order from AC-20.1\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"There is one orders row for buyer B1 with ORD-000001, date placed, address, deliveryOption NEXT_DAY, total 34.99, status Placed, and one order_lines row with partNumber BP-200, quantity 2, unitPrice 12.50\",\n     \"when\": \"the orders and order_lines tables are read\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"ORD-000001 exists\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned orderNumber is \\\"ORD-000002\\\"\",\n     \"when\": \"another valid order is placed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client sends unitPrice 1.00 for BP-200 priced £12.50\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The saved order_lines row has unitPrice 12.50, so the sent price value is ignored\",\n     \"when\": \"it calls POST /api/orders\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the buyer places an order with valid lines, address and delivery option, the orders API shall save an order with status Placed, a sequential order number ORD- followed by 6 zero-padded digits, each line's current part price as unit price, and total = subtotal + delivery charge.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-7\",\n    \"ASM-8\",\n    \"ASM-18\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Buyer B1\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400 and the orders table row count is unchanged\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 calls POST /api/orders with an empty lines list and otherwise valid fields\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Buyer B1\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Each response status is 400 with an error field naming the invalid input, and the orders table row count is unchanged\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 calls POST /api/orders with a 4-character address, then a 201-character address, then deliveryOption \\\"EXPRESS\\\", then quantity 0\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a place-order request has no lines, a quantity outside 1–99, an unknown part number, an address outside 5–200 characters, or a missing or unknown delivery option, then the orders API shall reject it with status 400 and save no order.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n   \"ears\": \"If any line's quantity is above the part's stock when an order is placed, then the orders API shall reject the order with status 409 and return each affected part number with the stock now available, saving no order.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-3\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-22.1\",\n     \"given\": \"Part BP-200 with stock 3 and part OF-100 with stock 0\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 calls POST /api/orders with BP-200 quantity 5 and OF-100 quantity 1\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 409, the response lists {BP-200, available 3} and {OF-100, available 0}, and the orders table row count is unchanged\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A buyer with 3 items in the cart and a valid address and delivery option\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-23.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"\\\"ORD-000007\\\" is displayed, the header cart count shows 0, and reloading /cart shows \\\"Your cart is empty\\\"\",\n     \"when\": \"they press \\\"Place order\\\" and the API returns ORD-000007\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an order is placed successfully, the portal shall empty the cart and show the new order number.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-23\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A buyer at checkout with 2 lines, an address and Next day selected, and the API returning status 500\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"An error message is shown, the 2 lines, the address and Next day are still displayed, and \\\"Place order\\\" is enabled\",\n     \"when\": \"they press \\\"Place order\\\"\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If placing an order fails with a network error or a server error, then the portal shall show an error message and keep the cart lines, address and delivery option so the buyer can try again.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-24\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-11\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Part BP-200 with stock 10\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-25.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The parts row for BP-200 still has stock value 10 after each call\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 places an order for 2 of BP-200 and then cancels it through the API\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The orders API shall leave the stock quantity in the parts database unchanged when an order is placed or cancelled.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-25\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"ASM-2\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"No session cookie, then an expired session token\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-26.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Each response status is 401 and no orders row is written\",\n     \"when\": \"GET /api/parts, POST /api/orders and GET /api/orders are called\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid session for buyer B1\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-26.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The saved orders row has buyer ID B1 read from the session, even if the request body sends a different buyer ID value\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 places an order\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to the API has no valid session token or cookie from the existing company login, then the API shall reject it with status 401.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-26\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-5\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Buyer B1 has 2 orders and buyer B2 has 3 orders\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-27.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned list has exactly B1's 2 orders\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 calls GET /api/orders\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Order ORD-000005 belongs to B2\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-27.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Each response status is 404 and the order row status is unchanged\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 calls GET /api/orders/ORD-000005 and POST /api/orders/ORD-000005/cancel\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The orders API shall return to a buyer only the orders placed by that buyer.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-27\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-5\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"B1 placed ORD-000001 on 1 Oct (2 filters + 1 pad) and ORD-000002 on 3 Oct\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-28.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned list is ORD-000002 then ORD-000001, and ORD-000001 has fields datePlaced, itemCount 3, total and status\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 calls GET /api/orders\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a buyer requests their orders, the orders API shall return them newest first, each with order number, date placed, number of items (total of all quantities), total and status.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-28\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-13\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"B1 has orders with statuses Placed, Placed and Cancelled\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-29.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned list has only the 1 Cancelled order\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 calls GET /api/orders?status=Cancelled\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the buyer picks a status filter on My orders, the orders API shall return only that buyer's orders with that status.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-29\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-6\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"B1's order ORD-000001 with 2 of BP-200 at £12.50, Next day, address \\\"1 High St, Leeds\\\"\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-30.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response has the line {BP-200, Brake Pad, 2, 12.50}, address \\\"1 High St, Leeds\\\", deliveryOption NEXT_DAY, total 34.99 and status Placed\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 calls GET /api/orders/ORD-000001\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a buyer opens one of their orders, the orders API shall return its lines (part number, name, quantity, unit price), delivery address, delivery option, total and status.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-30\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-6\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An order whose status was set to Dispatched in the database\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-31.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The timeline shown lists the four steps in order, and Dispatched is marked as current with a text label, not by colour alone\",\n     \"when\": \"the buyer opens it on My orders\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the buyer opens an order, the portal shall show a status timeline Placed → Packed → Dispatched → Delivered with the current status marked by text as well as colour.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-31\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"ASM-6\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An order with status Placed and one with status Packed\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-32.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"\\\"Cancel order\\\" is shown only for the Placed order\",\n     \"when\": \"the buyer opens each one\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The buyer pressed \\\"Cancel order\\\" on a Placed order\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-32.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"No cancel request is sent after declining; after confirming, the status shown becomes Cancelled and the button is no longer displayed\",\n     \"when\": \"they decline the confirmation, then press it again and confirm\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"While an order's status is Placed, the portal shall show a \\\"Cancel order\\\" button in the order detail that asks for confirmation before calling the cancel API.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-32\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"B1's order ORD-000001 with status Placed\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-33.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200, the response status field is \\\"Cancelled\\\", and the orders row has status Cancelled\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 calls POST /api/orders/ORD-000001/cancel\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a buyer cancels their order whose status is still Placed, the orders API shall set the status to Cancelled.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-33\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"B1's order ORD-000001 whose status was changed to Packed in the database\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-34.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 409 with an error message, and the orders row status is still Packed\",\n     \"when\": \"B1 calls POST /api/orders/ORD-000001/cancel\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The buyer has an order open showing Placed, and its status was changed to Packed in the database\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-34.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"A message is shown saying the order can no longer be cancelled, the panel refreshes to show Packed, and \\\"Cancel order\\\" is no longer displayed\",\n     \"when\": \"they press \\\"Cancel order\\\" and confirm\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If the order's status is no longer Placed when the buyer confirms cancelling, then the orders API shall refuse with status 409 and leave the status unchanged.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-34\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"ASM-10\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Buyer B3 with no orders\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-35.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned list is empty\",\n     \"when\": \"B3 calls GET /api/orders\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Buyer B3 with no orders\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-35.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"\\\"No orders yet\\\" and a link to /parts are shown\",\n     \"when\": \"they open /orders\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"While the buyer has no orders, the portal shall show \\\"No orders yet\\\" and a link to Find parts on My orders.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-35\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-36.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"No horizontal scroll bar is shown and every button and field is displayed and usable\",\n     \"when\": \"each screen is opened at 360 px, 768 px and 1280 px widths\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall show all three screens without horizontal scrolling at viewport widths from 360 px upwards.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-36\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"ASM-17\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The three screens with a cart containing 2 lines\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-37.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"Every step can be completed, focus is always visible, and every field has a label announced by a screen reader\",\n     \"when\": \"a tester uses only the keyboard to search, filter, add to cart, change quantity, remove, place an order, open an order and cancel it\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall give every form field a visible text label and let the buyer reach and use every control by keyboard alone.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-37\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-7\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"5,000 parts seeded in the parts database\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-38.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The 95th-percentile response time is under 500 ms and each response status is 200\",\n     \"when\": \"GET /api/parts?page=1&q=filter&category=Filters is called 100 times\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"5,000 parts seeded and a cold browser cache on a desktop with a 10 Mbps connection\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-38.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The first 20 parts are displayed within 2 seconds of navigation start\",\n     \"when\": \"a tester opens /parts\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"While the parts database holds 5,000 parts, the Find parts screen shall load its first page of results in under 2 seconds.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-38\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"ASM-16\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-39\",\n   \"ears\": \"When the orders API rejects an order with a 409 stock conflict, the cart shall lower each affected line to the stock now available with the message \\\"Only n available\\\", remove each affected line whose available stock is 0 with the message \\\"<part name> is now out of stock\\\", and keep all other lines.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-3\",\n    \"ASM-25\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-39.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A CartStore holding 5 of BP-200, 1 of OF-100 \\\"Oil Filter\\\" and 2 of AF-300\",\n     \"when\": \"CartStore.applyStockLimits([{BP-200, 3}, {OF-100, 0}]) is called with the 409 response\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned lines list has BP-200 with quantity value 3 and message \\\"Only 3 available\\\", AF-300 with quantity value 2, and no OF-100 line; the returned messages include \\\"Oil Filter is now out of stock\\\"\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-39.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The CartStore after AC-39.1\",\n     \"when\": \"CartStore.lines() is called\",\n     \"then\": \"Every returned line has a quantity value from 1 to 99 and CartStore.count() returns 5\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    }\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"metric\": \"95th-percentile time from navigation start until content is shown is under 2,000 ms for /parts, /cart and /orders, measured at 1,000 concurrent users\",\n   \"text\": \"Each of the three screens loads with 5,000 parts in the parts database.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n   \"metric\": \"Supports 1,000 buyers and 100,000 order and order-line records with NFR-1 still met\",\n   \"text\": \"Capacity for the first year.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n   \"metric\": \"0 serious or critical violations in an automated axe scan of each screen, plus 100% of fields with labels and 100% of stock and status indicators carrying text\",\n   \"text\": \"WCAG 2.1 AA compliance on all three screens; colour is never the only signal for stock state or order status.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"metric\": \"0 horizontal scroll at viewport widths of 360, 768 and 1280 px\",\n   \"text\": \"Responsive layout.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of ui and manual acceptance criteria pass on the latest 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox\",\n   \"text\": \"Browser support.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of prices shown as £ with exactly 2 decimals; 0 non-English text strings\",\n   \"text\": \"English only; prices in GBP.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"Sign-in and accounts (the existing company login is used as-is)\",\n  \"Payments and invoices\",\n  \"Admin or staff screens, including changing an order's status after Placed (ASM-6)\",\n  \"Adding or editing parts\",\n  \"Stock management, including changing stock when orders are placed or cancelled (ASM-2)\",\n  \"Returns\",\n  \"Emails and notifications\",\n  \"Multiple or saved delivery addresses (ASM-15)\",\n  \"Discounts\",\n  \"Vehicle (VIN) lookup\",\n  \"Reports\",\n  \"Mobile apps\",\n  \"Other languages or currencies\",\n  \"Integrations with other systems\"\n ],\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"ASM-19: The API endpoints are GET /api/parts (q, category, brand, page), GET /api/parts/brands, POST /api/orders, GET /api/orders (status), GET /api/orders/{orderNumber} and POST /api/orders/{orderNumber}/cancel. Paths can be renamed as long as the behaviour stays the same.\",\n  \"ASM-20: Cart and checkout logic in the React app sits in public client classes CartStore (addPart, setQuantity, removeLine, lines, count, subtotal, totals, applyStockLimits) and CheckoutForm (canPlaceOrder), so it can be unit-tested directly.\",\n  \"ASM-21: API error statuses are 400 for invalid input, 401 for no valid session, 404 for an order that doesn't exist or belongs to another buyer, and 409 for stock or cancel conflicts.\",\n  \"ASM-22: A quantity that isn't a whole number is rounded to the nearest whole number before being limited to 1–99 (from ASM-12).\",\n  \"ASM-23: Pressing \\\"Add to cart\\\" when the line quantity already equals the part's stock leaves the quantity unchanged and shows \\\"Only n available\\\", the same as REQ-14.\",\n  \"ASM-24: The order total is calculated on the server from current part prices and the delivery charge. Prices and totals the client sends are ignored.\",\n  \"ASM-25: When a 409 stock conflict shows a cart line's part now has 0 stock, the line is removed from the cart (rather than set to quantity 0) with the message \\\"<part name> is now out of stock\\\", so every remaining line keeps a quantity of 1–99 and the next order attempt is valid (refines ASM-3).\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nReview the spec."}